{"value": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/pulls/15785", "id": 3030445028, "node_id": "PR_kwDOAEfiCM60oOvk", "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/dubbo/pull/15785", "diff_url": "https://github.com/apache/dubbo/pull/15785.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/apache/dubbo/pull/15785.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/issues/15785", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/pulls/15785/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/pulls/15785/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/issues/15785/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/dubbo/statuses/c1326d64eda65ed94fe261379141db5c8221cb36", "number": 15785, "state": "closed", "locked": false, "title": "Fix: Stabilize multiple tests in `ServiceConfigTest` by isolating system properties and cached state", "user": {"login": "Anshul-creator", "id": 85193651, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTkzNjUx", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85193651?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator", "html_url": "https://github.com/Anshul-creator", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "## What is the purpose of the change?\r\n\r\nThis PR stabilizes several tests inside `ServiceConfigTest`:\r\n\r\n- `testMethodConfigWithInvalidArgumentIndex`\r\n- `testExport`\r\n- `testVersionAndGroupConfigFromProvider`\r\n- `testUnexport`\r\n- `testMethodConfigWithUnmatchedArgument`\r\n- `testMethodConfigWithUnknownArgumentType`\r\n- `testMethodConfigWithInvalidArgumentConfig`\r\n- `testMethodConfigWithConfiguredArgumentTypeAndIndex`\r\n- `testMethodConfigWithConfiguredArgumentType`\r\n- `testExportWithoutRegistryConfig`\r\n- `testDelayExport`\r\n- `testApplicationInUrl`\r\n- `testServiceListener`\r\n- `testProxy`\r\n- `testMethodConfigWithConfiguredArgumentIndex`\r\n\r\nThese tests were intermittently failing under randomized execution orders (NonDex). All of them involve the service export/unexport lifecycle and indirectly trigger application bootstrap logic, including the initialization of the metrics subsystem.\r\n\r\nWhen metrics are enabled, Micrometer\u2019s composite meter registry is created during bootstrap. Its internal data structures (such as `IdentityHashMap`) exhibit nondeterministic iteration behavior under random JVM execution orders, which leads to unpredictable test failures.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, `ServiceConfig` interacts with the global `DubboBootstrap` singleton, so any leftover state from one test can leak into the next one under random execution order.\r\n\r\n## Root Cause\r\n\r\nTwo independent sources of nondeterminism were affecting the tests:\r\n\r\n### 1. Metrics subsystem initialization\r\n\r\nEven though `ServiceConfigTest` does not test metrics functionality, the metrics subsystem is still initialized by default as part of the service export flow.\r\n\r\nMicrometer uses an `IdentityHashMap` internally, and under certain NonDex seeds this leads to exceptions such as:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\njava.lang.ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException\r\n  at java.util.IdentityHashMap$KeyIterator.next(...)\r\n  at io.micrometer.core.instrument.composite.CompositeMeterRegistry.updateDescendants(...)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis happens _before_ the test reaches any `ServiceConfig` assertions.\r\n\r\n### 2. Shared `DubboBootstrap` singleton\r\n\r\n`DubboBootstrap` stores global state such as exported services, protocol configuration, and application metadata.\r\n\r\nWithout cleanup between tests, the bootstrap instance from a previous test can leak into the next one, creating nondeterministic behavior under reordered execution.\r\n\r\n## Changes Made\r\n\r\nThe fix is as follows:\r\n\r\n- Metrics are explicitly disabled at the beginning of each test so that the metrics subsystem never initializes, removing one major source of nondeterminism.\r\n- All system properties introduced during testing are cleared afterward to prevent them from leaking across test boundaries.\r\n- The global Dubbo bootstrap instance is reset after every test to ensure complete isolation and eliminate interference caused by shared internal state.\r\n- No test logic, assertions, or mocks were modified.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\nYou can try running the following snippet of code from the dubbo repo root, on both pre-fix and post-fix code\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n./mvnw -q -pl dubbo-config/dubbo-config-api \\\r\n  edu.illinois:nondex-maven-plugin:2.2.1:nondex \\\r\n  -DnondexRuns=20\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe tests should fail intermittently on the pre-fix version, but pass consistently across all seeds on the post-fix version.\r\nNonDex run logs will be available under the `dubbo-config/dubbo-config-api/.nondex` directory.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n- [x] Make sure there is a [GitHub_issue](https://github.com/apache/dubbo/issues) field for the change.\r\n- [x] Write a pull request description that is detailed enough to understand what the pull request does, how, and why.\r\n- [x] Write necessary unit-test to verify your logic correction. If the new feature or significant change is committed, please remember to add sample in [dubbo samples](https://github.com/apache/dubbo-samples) project.\r\n- [x] Make sure gitHub actions can pass. [Why the workflow is failing and how to fix it?](../CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n", "labels": [], "milestone": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "created_at": "2025-11-20T15:58:26Z", "updated_at": "2025-11-21T18:49:26Z", "closed_at": "2025-11-21T06:50:56Z", "merged_at": "2025-11-21T06:50:56Z", "merge_commit_sha": "5e577c494858d7e0dc33f777c4d48ba970f53917", "assignee": null, "assignees": [], "requested_reviewers": [], "requested_teams": [], "head": {"label": "Anshul-creator:fix-ServiceConfigTest", "ref": "fix-ServiceConfigTest", "repo": {"id": 1076976850, "node_id": "R_kgDOQDFc0g", "name": "dubbo", "full_name": "Anshul-creator/dubbo", "owner": {"login": "Anshul-creator", "id": 85193651, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTkzNjUx", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85193651?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator", "html_url": "https://github.com/Anshul-creator", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Anshul-creator/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "private": false, "fork": true, "archived": false, "disabled": false, "description": "The java implementation of Apache Dubbo. An RPC and microservice framework.", "homepage": "https://dubbo.apac